236
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,081
<i>What are you doing?</i>

237
00:19:04,948 --> 00:19:07,200
- Shut it down! Come on!
- Weechai!

238
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,811
Chai! I told you to shut down the stream!

239
00:19:08,811 --> 00:19:11,899
Turn off the router, cut the power,
just shut everything down!

240
00:19:11,899 --> 00:19:14,541
We can't shut it down, sir.
Our feed's been hacked.

241
00:19:29,121 --> 00:19:35,160
<i>Well then, should we keep exposing
that evil old hag?</i>

242
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:36,961
<i>Good idea.</i>

243
00:19:40,507 --> 00:19:43,787
She can't be talking. She's dead!

244
00:19:43,787 --> 00:19:46,861
She can't! She can't be talking!

245
00:19:46,861 --> 00:19:50,211
I don't make mistakes.
I ordered to have you killed myself!

246
00:19:50,211 --> 00:19:52,371
I've never made a mistake.

247
00:19:52,371 --> 00:19:53,901
- I've never made a mistake!
- Mom!

248
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,558
- I've never made a mistake!
- Sir.

249
00:19:55,558 --> 00:19:57,477
They're in the parking lot.

250
00:19:57,477 --> 00:19:59,435
- Mom, you need to stop.
- I'm the one who had her killed.

251
00:19:59,435 --> 00:20:00,907
I'm the one who ordered to have her killed!

252
00:20:00,907 --> 00:20:03,984
Ginny, I ordered to have you killed myself!

253
00:20:03,984 --> 00:20:07,373
Everyone, please listen to me.

254
00:20:07,373 --> 00:20:12,445
Chanajit, Chaichana, and Weechana

255
00:20:12,445 --> 00:20:15,075
are connected to
the deaths of several people.

256
00:20:15,075 --> 00:20:17,261
Please don't let this be swept under the rug.

257
00:20:18,912 --> 00:20:21,600
Please don't let this be silenced.

258
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:25,101
Don't let this happen to anyone else.

259
00:20:28,557 --> 00:20:30,358
I'm in.

260
00:20:31,651 --> 00:20:36,325
Have you ever heard the saying
that the dead speak louder than the living?

261
00:20:36,325 --> 00:20:39,563
<i>If we can get someone to use AI
to bring Ginny back to life,</i>

262
00:20:39,563 --> 00:20:41,435
<i>it'll definitely get people talking.</i>

263
00:20:41,435 --> 00:20:43,501
<i>But we need to find someone
who can actually pull it off.</i>

264
00:20:43,501 --> 00:20:45,125
<i>Good idea.</i>

265
00:20:45,125 --> 00:20:46,373
<i>I think I can find someone.</i>

266
00:20:46,373 --> 00:20:48,331
That was so satisfying.

267
00:20:48,331 --> 00:20:50,661
Me too, Ginny.

268
00:20:55,952 --> 00:20:57,753
They are over there.

269
00:21:05,408 --> 00:21:07,209
Eva! Run!

270
00:22:37,704 --> 00:22:39,340
Eva?

271
00:22:53,104 --> 00:22:54,709
Pun!

272
00:22:54,709 --> 00:22:56,510
Watch out!

273
00:23:20,651 --> 00:23:22,452
Weechana?

274
00:24:21,539 --> 00:24:22,749
- Let us through.
- I didn't do it!

275
00:24:22,749 --> 00:24:24,344
- Let us through, please.
- It's not true!

276
00:24:24,344 --> 00:24:26,611
I didn't kill her! I didn't kill her!

277
00:24:26,611 --> 00:24:29,496
- I didn't kill her!
- Please move.

278
00:24:29,496 --> 00:24:32,867
I didn't kill her! I didn't kill her!

279
00:24:32,867 --> 00:24:36,181
<i>Weechana has been shot dead by police. Over.</i>

280
00:24:37,741 --> 00:24:40,301
Copy. Stand by.

281
00:24:43,421 --> 00:24:45,416
Weechana! My poor baby!

282
00:24:45,416 --> 00:24:47,299
Weechana!

283
00:24:52,053 --> 00:24:54,400
Weechana!

284
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:56,201
Excuse us.

285
00:25:08,021 --> 00:25:10,822
[Months later]

286
00:25:12,427 --> 00:25:13,989
I've been through...

287
00:25:13,989 --> 00:25:18,645
more than I can ever put into words
to get here today.

288
00:25:18,645 --> 00:25:22,779
There were so many moments I almost gave up,

289
00:25:22,779 --> 00:25:26,757
believing I wasn't good enough.

290
00:25:26,757 --> 00:25:30,587
But today,
I'm confident that if I'm given this role,

291
00:25:30,587 --> 00:25:35,483
I'll deliver a performance
that is complete and true

292
00:25:35,483 --> 00:25:37,401
in my own way.

293
00:25:48,430 --> 00:25:50,231
How was it?

294
00:25:50,936 --> 00:25:53,581
You good? You remember everything, right?

295
00:25:54,579 --> 00:25:59,021
And you can give them
even more than they're asking for, right?

296
00:26:02,475 --> 00:26:04,276
What did they say?

297
00:26:05,683 --> 00:26:08,181
I don't want it to be like this.

298
00:26:12,728 --> 00:26:14,613
It's okay.

299
00:26:14,613 --> 00:26:17,211
You did everything you could.

300
00:26:17,211 --> 00:26:19,617
You were amazing.

301
00:26:19,617 --> 00:26:21,065
Okay?

302
00:26:24,539 --> 00:26:26,821
It's okay, it's okay.

303
00:26:29,051 --> 00:26:31,901
I don't wanna go shoot overseas.

304
00:26:32,523 --> 00:26:34,324
I'm gonna miss you.

305
00:26:36,497 --> 00:26:37,795
What?

306
00:26:38,536 --> 00:26:40,135
They chose me.

307
00:26:40,135 --> 00:26:41,555
What?

308
00:26:41,555 --> 00:26:43,352
Oh my God, wait.

309
00:26:43,352 --> 00:26:45,347
Congrats, I'm so proud of you!

310
00:26:45,347 --> 00:26:47,923
Oh my God, congrats!

311
00:26:47,923 --> 00:26:50,802
You did it. You actually did it.

312
00:27:05,421 --> 00:27:08,222
Kiss him!

313
00:27:48,273 --> 00:27:49,869
Cut!

314
00:27:53,904 --> 00:27:56,101
Scene 14, Shot 1, Take 1.

315
00:27:56,101 --> 00:28:00,837
<i>Okay, so basically, I want to add more seats.</i>

316
00:28:00,837 --> 00:28:02,704
<i>Have you seen the old blueprint?</i>

317
00:28:02,704 --> 00:28:04,001
Wait.

318
00:28:04,001 --> 00:28:05,299
Ah, that's right.

319
00:28:05,299 --> 00:28:07,100
It's this one.

320
00:28:17,912 --> 00:28:21,144
The second one, you will be preparing
your guns in the backyard.

321
00:28:21,144 --> 00:28:23,888
And the rest will be discussed
a little bit later, okay?

322
00:28:23,888 --> 00:28:25,816
- Okay.
- Okay, great. Thank you.

323
00:28:25,816 --> 00:28:27,617
Thank you.

324
00:28:33,894 --> 00:28:35,000
Hello.

325
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:37,886
So the name is "Tasty Lean by Pun".

326
00:28:37,886 --> 00:28:39,912
It's good.

327
00:28:39,912 --> 00:28:41,699
Easy to understand.

328
00:28:41,699 --> 00:28:44,488
I just came up with a new recipe
for the restaurant's signature dessert.

329
00:28:44,488 --> 00:28:47,560
It's really good.
I'll make it for you when you get back.

330
00:28:50,130 --> 00:28:52,816
I miss you already.

331
00:28:52,816 --> 00:28:54,834
I miss you more.

332
00:28:54,834 --> 00:28:57,248
I miss you more and more.

333
00:28:57,248 --> 00:29:01,560
Can I call this dessert "Sweet Eva"?

334
00:29:04,544 --> 00:29:06,680
With my pleasure.

335
00:29:08,246 --> 00:29:10,673
Okay, I gotta go to work.

336
00:29:10,673 --> 00:29:12,960
Okay, bye.

337
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,145
Bye.

338
00:29:14,947 --> 00:29:17,270
- Can you hear my kisses?
- Yeah.

339
00:29:17,270 --> 00:29:18,746
Love you.

340
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:23,561
I'm gonna puke.

341
00:29:25,515 --> 00:29:27,562
You don't have a girlfriend.
You wouldn't know.

342
00:29:42,648 --> 00:29:43,923
<i>Hi, Eva.</i>

343
00:29:43,923 --> 00:29:48,304
<i>I just wanted to let you know
that Weechai and I are having a baby.</i>

344
00:29:48,304 --> 00:29:50,500
<i>So we're going to have a small wedding.</i>

345
00:29:50,500 --> 00:29:52,152
<i>We'd love for you to come if you're free.</i>

346
00:29:52,152 --> 00:29:53,350
<i>I'll send you an invitation.</i>

347
00:29:53,350 --> 00:29:55,151
<i>Bye.</i>

348
00:30:10,880 --> 00:30:13,355
[One year later]

349
00:30:29,270 --> 00:30:30,755
Is this the salmon steak for Table Two?

350
00:30:30,755 --> 00:30:31,928
- That's right.
- Ready?

351
00:30:31,928 --> 00:30:33,729
- It's ready.
- Okay.

352
00:30:34,942 --> 00:30:36,318
What about this one?

353
00:30:36,318 --> 00:30:37,406
Is this the mushroom pesto pasta?

354
00:30:37,406 --> 00:30:38,456
- That's right.
- For Table Seven?

355
00:30:38,456 --> 00:30:39,496
That's right.

356
00:30:39,496 --> 00:30:42,136
- Did you weigh the chicken?
- I already did.

357
00:30:42,136 --> 00:30:44,643
Okay, make it look nice.

358
00:30:44,643 --> 00:30:48,864
The mushroom pesto pasta for Table Seven.

359
00:30:48,864 --> 00:30:50,440
Hey.

360
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:52,900
The customer at Table 11
wants to make a complaint.

361
00:30:53,798 --> 00:30:55,599
About what?

362
00:30:56,475 --> 00:30:59,488
They just said you need to go out there
and deal with it yourself.

363
00:30:59,488 --> 00:31:00,901
Me?

364
00:31:41,835 --> 00:31:44,200
Is something wrong?

365
00:31:45,691 --> 00:31:49,315
I'd like to make a complaint about the owner.

366
00:31:49,315 --> 00:31:52,200
Whatever the complaint is,
let's take it easy, okay?

367
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:53,816
No, I can't.

368
00:31:53,816 --> 00:31:56,478
I want the restaurant to have more days off.

369
00:31:56,478 --> 00:32:00,200
The owner works way too much.
He never has time for his girlfriend.

370
00:32:01,131 --> 00:32:02,932
I simply can't allow that.

371
00:32:03,915 --> 00:32:06,118
I missed you.

372
00:32:06,118 --> 00:32:07,919
Eva.

373
00:32:12,392 --> 00:32:14,904
I said I missed you.

374
00:32:22,323 --> 00:32:23,796
Okay.

375
00:32:26,553 --> 00:32:27,976
Let's go.

376
00:32:35,206 --> 00:32:37,007
Excuse me.

377
00:32:38,777 --> 00:32:41,617
That's my friend. He's my friend.

378
00:33:48,950 --> 00:33:51,200
Do you want me to be closer to you?

379
00:33:53,366 --> 00:33:55,232
What do you mean?

380
00:33:55,232 --> 00:33:58,616
Like... maybe I could open
a restaurant in Bangkok.

381
00:33:58,616 --> 00:34:00,417
That way, we could be closer to each other.

382
00:34:01,928 --> 00:34:03,731
I mean, I'd love that.

383
00:34:03,731 --> 00:34:07,784
But you should get everything
sorted out here first.

384
00:34:07,784 --> 00:34:09,878
I can always come see you.

385
00:34:10,696 --> 00:34:14,403
The restaurant's doing pretty well now.
We're busy every day.

386
00:34:14,403 --> 00:34:17,500
I've been thinking about opening
a second location anyway.

387
00:34:18,540 --> 00:34:20,341
What's the rush?

388
00:34:22,667 --> 00:34:24,214
Well...

389
00:34:25,446 --> 00:34:27,247
I wanna get married.

390
00:34:29,047 --> 00:34:30,848
What did you say?

391
00:34:32,158 --> 00:34:35,638
Big stars don't say yes to marriage
that easily, do they?

392
00:34:35,638 --> 00:34:37,555
Well, depends on which star.

393
00:34:37,555 --> 00:34:38,899
What about this one?

394
00:34:38,899 --> 00:34:40,413
Depends on who I'm marrying.

395
00:34:40,413 --> 00:34:42,214
Well, what about me?

396
00:34:49,448 --> 00:34:51,249
Honestly,

397
00:34:52,088 --> 00:34:54,595
I don't really wanna get married.

398
00:34:54,595 --> 00:34:56,035
But...

399
00:34:56,035 --> 00:34:59,063
I just want delicious,
healthy food for every meal.

400
00:34:59,063 --> 00:35:00,389
And?

401
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:05,318
It'd be nice

402
00:35:05,318 --> 00:35:07,240
to have a chef around all the time,
don't you think?

403
00:35:08,352 --> 00:35:10,326
What does it mean?

404
00:35:10,326 --> 00:35:12,544
It means I'm saying yes.

405
00:35:12,544 --> 00:35:14,360
You need to find me a ring.

406
00:35:57,067 --> 00:35:59,000
Will you marry me?

407
00:35:59,990 --> 00:36:02,007
Absolutely.

408
00:36:41,099 --> 00:36:44,238
My wife! My wife!

409
00:36:53,709 --> 00:36:55,128
Can you say it with a Thai flair?

410
00:36:55,128 --> 00:36:56,328
My 'mia'.

411
00:36:56,328 --> 00:36:58,129
My 'pua'.
